# Gotchas only

A **gotcha** is a specific claim in a pleading or affidavit that hard evidence in another case document proves false. Quote both. If both can be true, do not flag.

**Flag:** “never received notice” vs certified-mail receipt; “no income” vs pay records; “never knew” vs a letter they were sent; “did not sign” vs a notarized signature; arithmetic on a statement that cannot add up.

**Do not flag:** mortgage dated vs recorded; 4.5% vs 4.6%; $318,000 vs $318,500; Jose vs J.; NYSCEF headers; overlapping party names on unrelated exhibits; anything that is a discrepancy rather than a lie.
